{"id":"11f68c1f6dba64ff","group":"93","path":"93/93-thm-unique-algebra.md","title":"Unique Algebra Theorem","display":"Unique Algebra Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-thm-unique-algebra","aliases":["93-thm-unique-algebra"],"display":"Unique Algebra Theorem","depends_on":["[[93-df-algebraizable]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-thm-unique-algebra"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-thm-unique-algebra</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Unique Algebra Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a55351eb48f8bd69\" href=\"?note=a55351eb48f8bd69\" title=\"93-df-algebraizable\">93-df-algebraizable</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"thm-unique-algebra-—-Unique-Algebra-Theorem\">thm-unique-algebra — Unique Algebra Theorem</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L\">\\(\\mathcal L\\)</span> is a fixed logic with algebraic signature <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathcal L}\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathcal L}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathcal K_i;\\tau_{\\mathcal L})\">\\(\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathcal K_i;\\tau_{\\mathcal L})\\)</span> is the equivalent-algebraic-semantics predicate of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"a55351eb48f8bd69\" href=\"?note=a55351eb48f8bd69\" title=\"93-df-algebraizable\">93-df-algebraizable</a>; it already requires each <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal K_i\">\\(\\mathcal K_i\\)</span> to be a quasivariety of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathcal L}\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathcal L}\\)</span>-algebras.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}unique\\text{-}algebra}\\vdash \\Bigl(\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathcal K_1;\\tau_{\\mathcal L})\\land\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathcal K_2;\\tau_{\\mathcal L})\\Bigr)\\to\\mathcal K_1=\\mathcal K_2\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}unique\\text{-}algebra}\\vdash \\Bigl(\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathcal K_1;\\tau_{\\mathcal L})\\land\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathcal K_2;\\tau_{\\mathcal L})\\Bigr)\\to\\mathcal K_1=\\mathcal K_2\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>The equivalent algebraic semantics of a fixed algebraizable logic is unique as a quasivariety in its fixed algebraic signature.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"thm-unique-algebra-—-Unique-Algebra-Theorem","text":"thm-unique-algebra — Unique Algebra Theorem","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-algebraizable","status":"resolved","id":"a55351eb48f8bd69","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-algebraizable]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-algebraizable","status":"resolved","id":"a55351eb48f8bd69","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathcal K_i;\\tau_{\\mathcal L})$ is the equivalent-algebraic-semantics predicate of [[93-df-algebraizable]]; it already requires each $\\mathcal K_i$ to be a quasivariety of $\\tau_{\\mathcal L}$-algebras.","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathcal L","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_{\\mathcal L}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathcal K_i;\\tau_{\\mathcal L})","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal K_i","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_{\\mathcal L}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}unique\\text{-}algebra}\\vdash \\Bigl(\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathcal K_1;\\tau_{\\mathcal L})\\land\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathcal K_2;\\tau_{\\mathcal L})\\Bigr)\\to\\mathcal K_1=\\mathcal K_2","display":true}],"bytes":970,"backlinks":[],"outgoing":["a55351eb48f8bd69"]}